    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d703">

                <pb facs="0563" n="481" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg481"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 702.1211/213.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexican Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1358.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor and regret to
                    apprise your excellency that, according to a report from the consul of Mexico at
                    Douglas, <pb facs="0564" n="482" xml:id="pg482"/> Ariz., a group of rebels
                    yesterday stood in front of the consulate and insulted the personnel of that
                    office whenever they came out on the street.</p>
                <p>The local authorities know of this, and in view of the gravity of the offense I
                    hasten to bring it to your excellency’s knowledge, feeling assured that you will
                    please to issue such orders as may be necessary to secure the personnel of the
                    Mexican consulate at Douglas from such annoyances on the territory of this
                    friendly nation.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. de Zamacona.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
